# Commits to skip in `git blame` — bulk mechanical reformats only.
#
# Enable locally with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Nothing goes in here that a reviewer would want blame to stop on. A commit
# qualifies only if it changed no behaviour and applied no rule by hand — the
# output of `biome format` and nothing else. That is why #20 landed as three
# commits (config, format, lint fixes) rather than one: only the middle one is
# listed here, so blaming the suppression comments and the config still lands
# on the commit that reasoned about them.
#
# SHAs are added *after* merge. GitHub rewrites commit SHAs on rebase-merge, so
# a branch-local SHA recorded before merge would point at an object that never
# reaches main.

# 1.2b — apply the initial Biome format pass (#20)
